{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27928,"name":"The Notes Publisher","username":"The_Notes_Publisher","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/the_notes_publisher/{size}/12422_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-28T08:18:48.822Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSpark Program 和 Community Fund DAO 加起来已经有三年的资助历史，但今天想把它读明白，只能一个帖子一个帖子地翻。提案、公示、结项报告、终止公告——全都在 \u003ca href=\"http://talk.nervos.org\"\u003etalk.nervos.org\u003c/a\u003e 上，散落在 260 多个帖子里。想知道 Spark 在 2025 年到底资助了什么，或者三月提的 DAO 提案现在什么状态，你得开二十个标签页，耗掉一个下午。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e所以我做了这个索引。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e已经上线： \u003ca href=\"https://thenotespublisher.github.io/ckb-funding-tracker/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Funding Tracker\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e两个资助板块的全部帖子，从 Discourse API 拉取、脚本自动分类（提案 / 公示 / 结项报告 / 终止 / 治理），可搜索、可筛选。一条命令就能从论坛实况重建整本账——没有任何人工维护，分类规则就是三十行正则，任何人都能读、都能来挑毛病。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e目前索引里的数字：Spark 提案 88 条、公示 12 条、结项报告 7 份、终止 1 条；DAO 提案 83 条，最早到 2023 年 1 月。其中 2026 年就占了 153 条——资助不但没停，反而在加速，只是从来没有人把它汇编成一本账。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e这次提案想做的，是把它维护下去，做成两个基金都配得上的账本：\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 按社区意见修正分类错漏\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 给每个有仓库的受资助项目补上 GitHub 链接\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 每日 CI 刷新 + \"本周变化\"视图，评审和社区一眼看到动向\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 开一个所有人可消费的 JSON 接口\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e关于前人工作，先说清楚，因为功课我做足了：Build-Union 在 2025 年 8 月拿到 Spark 资助做了 Grant-Tracking-Platform（t/8952，结项报告 t/9725）。那个仓库从 2025 年 12 月起就停更了，vercel 部署也停在旧状态。我不打算装作它不存在——我更愿意公开把这条线捡起来，做成一个静态、零后端、可复跑的账本，哪天我不干了，社区自己就能接手维护。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e为什么是我：独立开发者，全程用 AI coding agent 交付——这个追踪器（抓取脚本、分类、站点）就是这么做出来的，这恰好是 agent 最擅长的那类流水线。此前在 Neo N3 生态维护工具链（neo-mamba，NEO3 的 Python SDK；neofs-python-sdk，NeoFS 存储 SDK——都是活仓库）。第一次申请 CKB 资助，我更愿意带着能跑的东西来，而不是一张承诺。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e为什么是现在：透明度的问题一再被提起（DAO 投票数据 t/11246、公平性讨论、Spark 自己的 Q1/Q2 复盘）。在下一波提案到来之前，一个常设索引是两个基金的基本盘。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e预算：$700，一个月：\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 第 1 周 — 修正分类 + 补受资助项目的 GitHub 链接\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 第 2 周 — 每日 CI 刷新 + 周度变化视图\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 第 3 周 — JSON 接口 + 文档\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- 第 4 周 — 结项报告，把账本移交 给愿意接手的社区成员\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e仓库：\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/thenotespublisher/ckb-funding-tracker%EF%BC%88MIT%EF%BC%8C%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%80%E5%A4%A9%E8%B5%B7%E5%B0%B1%E5%85%AC%E5%BC%80%EF%BC%89\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://github.com/thenotespublisher/ckb-funding-tracker（MIT，第一天起就公开）\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e联系：站内 DM 即可，中文/英文都行。\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e================================================================\u003cbr\u003e\nThe Spark Program and the Community Fund DAO have three years of funding history between them, and the only way to read it today is one forum thread at a time. Proposals, funding announcements, completion reports, terminations — all of it on \u003ca href=\"http://talk.nervos.org\"\u003etalk.nervos.org\u003c/a\u003e, scattered across 260+ topics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo I built the index. Live now: \u003ca href=\"https://thenotespublisher.github.io/ckb-funding-tracker/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Funding Tracker\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery topic from both funding categories, pulled from the Discourse API, classified by script (proposal / funded / report / terminated / governance), searchable, filterable. One command rebuilds the whole ledger — nothing hand-maintained, classification is thirty lines of regex anyone can argue with.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNumbers so far: 88 Spark proposals, 12 funded announcements, 7 completion reports, 1 termination; 83 DAO proposals back to January 2023. 153 of those topics are from 2026 alone — funding isn’t slowing down; it’s accelerating, and nobody had put it in one ledger.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis proposal is to keep it alive:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Fix classification where the community says the tags are wrong\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Add GitHub links for every funded project that has a repo\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Daily CI refresh + a “changed this week” view\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- A JSON endpoint anyone can consume\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrior work, stated plainly: Build-Union received Spark funding in Aug 2025 for a Grant-Tracking-Platform (t/8952, completion report t/9725). The repo has been dormant since Dec 2025. I’d rather pick that thread back up in public — as a static, zero-backend, re-runnable ledger the community can maintain if I get hit by a bus.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy me: independent builder, shipping with AI coding agents end-to-end — this tracker was built that way. I maintain tooling in the Neo N3 ecosystem (neo-mamba, a Python SDK for NEO3; neofs-python-sdk). First CKB grant; I’d rather show up with a working product than a promise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy now: the transparency question keeps coming up (DAO voting in numbers t/11246, the fairness threads, Spark’s own retrospectives). A standing index is table stakes before the next wave of proposals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBudget: $700, one month:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- week 1: classification fixes + GitHub links\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- week 2: daily CI refresh + weekly diff view\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- week 3: JSON endpoint + docs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- week 4: closing report, handover to the community\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepo: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/thenotespublisher/ckb-funding-tracker\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - thenotespublisher/ckb-funding-tracker · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e (MIT, public from day one)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eContact: DM here on Nervos Talk.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-11-28T08:18:48.822Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":14,"readers_count":13,"score":